IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-convention-scope`
IMPORT `caa-convention-liability`

-- Carriage by Air Act 1988, sections 1 to 13.  Source: source/CAA1988.txt lines 16 to 245.
--
-- The Act gives the force of law to the three texts of the Warsaw Convention set out in the
-- Schedules and adds seven rules of its own (ss 5 to 11).  The Convention articles are in
-- caa-convention-scope.l4, caa-convention-liability.l4 and caa-convention-final.l4.

§ `The Act`

§§ `1. Short title`

-- Inert: names the Act.

§§ `2. Interpretation`

-- The definitions of "Hague Protocol", "Montreal Protocol No. 4", "Warsaw Convention",
-- "Warsaw (Hague) Convention" and "Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention" name the three texts
-- in the Second, First and Third Schedules: they are the `Convention` input.  "Court" includes
-- an arbitrator in an arbitration the Convention allows.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 2 'court'"
GIVEN a IS AN `Arbitration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arbitrator is the court` IF
        a's `the proceedings are an arbitration`
    AND a's `the arbitration is allowed by a Convention`

§§ `3. Conventions to have force of law`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 3(1)"
GIVEN f IS A `Force of Law Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore in relation to the carriage` IF
        f's `the provisions relate to the rights and liabilities of carriers, carriers' employees and agents, passengers, consignors, consignees or other persons`
    AND f's `the carriage is carriage by air to which the Convention applies`

-- 3(2): if a text in a Schedule is inconsistent with the authentic French text of the
-- Convention or Protocol, the French text prevails.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 3(2)"
GIVEN `a text set out in a Schedule is inconsistent with the authentic French text` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authentic French text prevails` IF
    `a text set out in a Schedule is inconsistent with the authentic French text`

§§ `4. High Contracting Parties`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 4(1)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN s IS A `State Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State is a High Contracting Party to the Convention` IF
    s's `the State has ratified or acceded to the Convention`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 4(1)(d)"
GIVEN s IS A `State Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to the High Contracting Party in respect of the territory` IF
        `the State is a High Contracting Party to the Convention` s
    AND s's `the State is a party to the Convention in respect of the territory`

-- 4(1)(e): this Act applies to a High Contracting Party "to the extent that it has availed
-- itself of the provisions of the Additional Protocol".  Read with the Additional Protocol,
-- which lets a party declare that Article 2(1) does not apply to international carriage
-- performed directly by the State, the Act does not apply to such carriage where the party
-- has so declared (NOTES.md fork F1).

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 4(1)(e)"
GIVEN s IS A `State Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to carriage performed directly by the High Contracting Party` IF
        `the State is a High Contracting Party to the Convention` s
    AND NOT s's `the State has availed itself of the provisions of the Additional Protocol`

-- 4(2): Article 40A(2) (First and Third Schedules) is not to be read as extending references
-- to the territory of a High Contracting Party, other than references to the territory of any
-- State, to territory in respect of which that party is not a party.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 4(2)"
GIVEN `the reference is to the territory of any State, whether or not a High Contracting Party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the High Contracting Party is a party in respect of the territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 40A(2) extends the reference to include the territory` IF
        `the reference is to the territory of any State, whether or not a High Contracting Party`
     OR `the High Contracting Party is a party in respect of the territory`

§§ `5. Fatal accidents`

-- References in s 20 of the Civil Law Act 1909 to a wrongful act, neglect or default include
-- any occurrence which gives rise to liability under Article 17.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 5"
GIVEN p IS A `Passenger Accident Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occurrence is a wrongful act, neglect or default for the purposes of section 20 of the Civil Law Act 1909` IF
    `the carrier is liable under Article 17` p

§§ `6. Limitations of liability`

-- 6(1): the limitations in Article 22 apply whatever the nature of the proceedings, and the
-- limit for each passenger applies to the aggregate liability of the carrier in all proceedings
-- in Singapore together with any brought outside Singapore.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(1)"
`the limitations on liability in Article 22 apply whatever the nature of the proceedings by which liability may be enforced` MEANS TRUE

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(1)"
GIVEN `the passenger limit` IS A NUMBER
      l IS A `Limited Proceedings Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount still recoverable within the limit for each passenger` MEANS
    IF `the passenger limit` MINUS sum (l's `the amounts awarded or recoverable in those other proceedings`) LESS THAN 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the passenger limit` MINUS sum (l's `the amounts awarded or recoverable in those other proceedings`)

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(2)"
GIVEN l IS A `Limited Proceedings Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may at any stage make an order that is just and equitable in view of Article 22` IF
    l's `the proceedings enforce a liability limited by Article 22`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(3)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN l IS A `Limited Proceedings Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may award less than it would have awarded or make part of its award conditional on other proceedings` IF
        l's `the proceedings enforce a liability limited by Article 22`
    AND l's `the liability is or may be partly enforceable in other proceedings in Singapore or elsewhere`

-- 6(4): the Minister may by order specify the amounts equivalent to the sums in francs or
-- Special Drawing Rights.  No order is an input; with none the conversion has no answer.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(4)"
GIVEN `the sum in francs or Special Drawing Rights` IS A NUMBER
      e IS AN `Equivalent Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF e's `the Minister has by order specified an equivalent in Singapore dollars for one unit`
    THEN `the sum in francs or Special Drawing Rights` TIMES e's `the equivalent in Singapore dollars of one unit specified by the order`
    ELSE REFUSE "no order under section 6(4) specifying the equivalent in Singapore dollars of the sums in francs or Special Drawing Rights is encoded in this model"

-- 6(5): references to Article 22 include Article 22 as applied by Article 25A: a rule of
-- construction, inert.

§§ `7. Notice of partial loss`

-- In Article 26(2), references to damage include loss of part of the baggage or cargo, and
-- references to receipt, in relation to loss of part, are to receipt of the remainder.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 7(a)"
`for Article 26(2) damage includes loss of part of the baggage or cargo` MEANS TRUE

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 7(b)"
GIVEN p IS A `Partial Loss Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date of receipt for Article 26(2)` MEANS
    IF p's `part of the baggage or cargo is lost`
    THEN p's `the date the remainder was received`
    ELSE p's `the date the whole was received`

§§ `8. Time for bringing proceedings`

-- 8(1): no action against a carrier's employee or agent arising out of damage to which a
-- Convention relates, if the employee or agent was acting within the scope of employment, may
-- be brought after more than 2 years, reckoned from the date of arrival, or from the date the
-- aircraft ought to have arrived, or from the date the carriage stopped.  8(4): "action"
-- includes an arbitration.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 8(1) and (4)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Employee Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` IF
        a's `the action arises out of damage to which a Convention relates`
    AND a's `the action is against the carrier's employee or agent`
    AND a's `the employee or agent was acting within the scope of his or her employment`
    AND a's `the date the action or arbitration is brought`
        GREATER THAN `the last day for bringing the action` (a's `how the carriage ended`)

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 8(2)"
`Article 29 applies to proceedings for contribution between persons liable for damage to which a Convention relates` MEANS FALSE

-- 8(3): subject to ss 4 and 29 of the Limitation Act 1959, no contribution action may be
-- brought after 2 years from the time a court gives judgment or makes an award against the
-- person seeking contribution.  The extension the Limitation Act allows is an input.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 8(3) and (4)"
GIVEN k IS A `Contribution Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution action is in time` IF
    NOT k's `the person seeks to recover contribution in respect of damage to which a Convention relates`
    OR k's `the date the action or arbitration for contribution is brought`
        AT MOST `add months` (k's `the date the court gave judgment or made an award against the person seeking contribution`) 24
    OR (CONSIDER k's `the last day allowed by sections 4 and 29 of the Limitation Act 1959, where they extend the time`
        WHEN JUST extended THEN k's `the date the action or arbitration for contribution is brought` AT MOST extended
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

§§ `9. Contributory negligence`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 9"
`the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953 is a law of Singapore under which a court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly for the purposes of Article 21` MEANS TRUE

§§ `10. Power to exclude aircraft in use for military purposes`

-- 10(1): the Minister may by order direct that the section applies, or ceases to apply, to
-- Singapore or another State.  10(2): the Warsaw (Hague) and Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal)
-- Conventions do not apply to the carriage of persons, cargo and baggage for the military
-- authorities of a State to which the section applies in aircraft registered in that State if
-- the whole capacity has been reserved by or on behalf of those authorities.  The Warsaw
-- Convention (Second Schedule) is not mentioned.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 10(1) and (2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      m IS A `Military Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            m's `the Minister has by order directed that section 10 applies to the State`
        AND m's `the carriage is of persons, cargo or baggage for the military authorities of that State`
        AND m's `the aircraft is registered in that State`
        AND m's `the whole capacity of the aircraft has been reserved by or on behalf of those authorities`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            m's `the Minister has by order directed that section 10 applies to the State`
        AND m's `the carriage is of persons, cargo or baggage for the military authorities of that State`
        AND m's `the aircraft is registered in that State`
        AND m's `the whole capacity of the aircraft has been reserved by or on behalf of those authorities`

§§ `11. Actions against High Contracting Parties`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 11(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Party Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Contracting Party is deemed to have submitted to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` IF
        p's `the State is a High Contracting Party to a Convention`
    AND NOT p's `the State has availed itself of the provisions of the Additional Protocol`
    AND p's `the action is brought in a court in Singapore in accordance with Article 28`
    AND p's `the claim is in respect of carriage undertaken by the High Contracting Party`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 11(2)"
`section 11 authorises the issue of an enforcement order against the property of the High Contracting Party` MEANS FALSE

§§ `12. Application to carriage by air not governed by Warsaw (Hague) Convention and Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`

-- The Minister may make regulations applying the First and Third Schedules and any provision
-- of the Act to carriage that is not international carriage.  No regulations are an input, and
-- the section supplies no fallback.

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 12"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 12 applying the First and Third Schedules to carriage other than international carriage are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 12 applying the First and Third Schedules to carriage other than international carriage are encoded in this model"

§§ `13. Application to Government`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 13"
`this Act binds the Government` MEANS TRUE
